#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Shut down iOS Simulators that nothing has used for a while.

    sim-janitor run [--dry-run] [--grace-minutes N] [--session-idle-minutes N]
    sim-janitor status [--grace-minutes N] [--session-idle-minutes N]
    sim-janitor lease UDID -- COMMAND...      hold the device while COMMAND runs

A machine-wide backstop that knows nothing about any one app. launchd runs one
short pass every 5 minutes. Each pass lists the booted devices in the default
device set and in `--set testing`, where XCTest keeps its parallel-testing
clones, and decides whether each one is in use. Any of these marks a device in
use:

  - a held lease: `sim-janitor lease` holds a shared flock on
    ~/Library/Caches/sim-janitor/leases/<UDID>.lock while its command runs;
  - a process outside the simulators' own runtime trees (each launchd_sim and
    its descendants) whose argv names the UDID, such as xcodebuild
    `-destination id=`, `xcrun simctl` subcommands, maestro or agent-device;
  - a process outside those trees with a `-destination` whose `name=` is the
    device's exact name, as in xcodebuild
    `-destination 'platform=iOS Simulator,name=iPhone 17'`. It owns every
    booted device with that name;
  - a process in the device's own tree that is being traced (ps stat `X`),
    which is a debugger attached to an app or test runner;
  - an agent-device claim in ~/.agent-device/device-claims (or
    $AGENT_DEVICE_CLAIMS_DIR) whose owner process is still running with the
    start time the claim records, that agent-device has not marked abandoned,
    and whose session shows activity within the session cap (2 hours;
    SIM_JANITOR_SESSION_IDLE_MINUTES or --session-idle-minutes). A session's
    last activity is the later of the claim's updatedAtMs and the mtime of
    <stateDir>/sessions/<session>/events.ndjson, where the daemon appends a
    line as each request on the session starts and finishes. If either cannot
    be read the claim counts as in use. A transient-command claim, held for one
    command and abandoned after it, counts while its owner runs.

The device's own tree also gives activity, which only delays a shutdown: the
newest start time of an app (a main executable under
/Containers/Bundle/Application/), a test runner (`*-Runner.app`) or `xctest`
process there counts as the device's last use. App extensions and simulator
system daemons do not count, since the system restarts them on its own. A
running app's start time counts, not its existence, so an app left open does
not keep a device forever.

An agent-device runner (the detached `xcodebuild test-without-building` of
AgentDeviceRunner) is not an owner by itself, because one whose session is
gone would pin its device forever. While its session is open and active the
claim keeps the device. The janitor never stops a runner; shutting the device
down ends it.

A clone in the testing set ("Clone N of NAME") is also owned through the
default-set device NAME, since xcodebuild names only the source device.

A device is shut down with `xcrun simctl shutdown` once it has been idle for
longer than the grace period (30 minutes; SIM_JANITOR_GRACE_MINUTES or
--grace-minutes). Idle time runs from the latest of the last pass that saw an
owner, the device's boot, and the newest app or test start in its tree. A
device seen for the first time is idle from that moment. The janitor never
deletes or erases a device, never touches one that is not Booted, and never
signals any process other than its own hung subprocesses.

Right before each shutdown the janitor takes an exclusive flock on the
device's lease file, and on its source device's for a clone, creating the
file if needed (it never deletes one). Holding those, it lists the devices,
reads the process table and the claims again, and judges that device afresh,
so an owner that arrived during an earlier shutdown, or a reboot, keeps it. It
keeps the locks until `simctl shutdown` returns or times out, then writes the
outcome into the lease file. A `sim-janitor lease` started meanwhile waits for
the locks, at most one final check and one shutdown timeout, says on stderr
that the janitor shut the device down while it waited if it did, and then runs
its command anyway.

Every subprocess has a hard timeout, capped at what is left of the pass's
budget, since simctl hangs when CoreSimulatorService is overloaded. Devices are
tried least recently failed first, and one whose shutdown failed twice in a
row waits 10 minutes, doubling to an hour, so it can't starve the others. Only
one pass runs at a time (a non-blocking flock). Every pass logs at least one
line to ~/Library/Logs/sim-janitor.log. If ~/.agents/sim-janitor.pause exists
a pass logs that and exits, and a pass that sees it appear stops before its
next shutdown. If the process table or the claim directory cannot be read,
the pass keeps every device.

What it cannot see, so hold a lease or pause it for these:

  - a person using Simulator.app by hand, with no tool attached and no app
    launched within the grace period;
  - an Xcode GUI run or test longer than the grace period with no debugger
    attached, since Xcode's own argv names no device;
  - a long run of a tool that names the device some other way, such as
    `maestro test` without `--device` or `simctl ... booted`, once its app or
    test runner started more than the grace period ago;
  - an agent-device session silent for longer than the session cap;
  - the command of a `lease` whose wrapper was killed with SIGKILL, since the
    kernel drops the flock with the wrapper.

And what it trusts: any long-lived process that names the UDID (a forgotten
`simctl io recordVideo`, `log stream`) or the device's name in a
`-destination` pins it until it exits. `status` names each one. Idle clocks
and shutdown failures live in a cache file, so losing it only restarts them.
"""
import argparse
import errno
import fcntl
import json
import os
from pathlib import Path
import re
import signal
import subprocess
import sys
import time
import traceback

UDID = re.compile(r'[0-9A-Fa-f]{8}-[0-9A-Fa-f]{4}-[0-9A-Fa-f]{4}-[0-9A-Fa-f]{4}-[0-9A-Fa-f]{12}')
CLONE = re.compile(r'Clone \d+ of (.+)')
LOG_LIMIT = 1 << 20
# A claim file that cannot be parsed may be half written. One this young still
# counts as an owner, an older one is reported and ignored so it can't pin.
UNREADABLE_CLAIM_WINDOW = 300
CLAIM_LIMIT = 1 << 16
# After two shutdown failures in a row a device waits this long, doubling per
# further failure up to the cap, so one wedged device can't take every pass.
BACKOFF_BASE = 600
BACKOFF_MAX = 3600
# A main app executable (not an extension under PlugIns/), a UI test runner,
# or xctest. Their start times are activity on the device.
BUNDLE_APP = re.compile(r'/Containers/Bundle/Application/[0-9A-Fa-f-]{36}/[^/]+\.app/[^/ ]+(?: |$)')
TEST_RUNNER = re.compile(r'-Runner\.app/[^/ ]+(?: |$)|(?:^|/)xctest(?: |$)')
DESTINATION = re.compile(r'(?:^|\s)-destination(?:=|\s+)')
DESTINATION_END = re.compile(r'\s+(?:-{1,2}[A-Za-z]|[|;&])')


class Unavailable(Exception):
    """A subprocess failed, timed out, or printed something unexpected."""


class PassDeadline(Exception):
    pass


def env_float(name, default):
    try:
        return float(os.environ[name])
    except (KeyError, ValueError):
        return default


class Config:
    """Every path and limit the janitor uses, so tests can point them elsewhere."""

    def __init__(self, home=None, **overrides):
        home = Path(home or os.environ.get('SIM_JANITOR_HOME') or Path.home())
        state_dir = Path(os.environ.get('SIM_JANITOR_STATE_DIR') or home / 'Library/Caches/sim-janitor')
        self.state_dir = state_dir
        self.lease_dir = state_dir / 'leases'
        self.state_file = state_dir / 'state.json'
        self.lock_file = state_dir / 'janitor.lock'
        self.log_file = Path(os.environ.get('SIM_JANITOR_LOG') or home / 'Library/Logs/sim-janitor.log')
        self.pause_file = Path(os.environ.get('SIM_JANITOR_PAUSE') or home / '.agents/sim-janitor.pause')
        claims = [home / '.agent-device/device-claims']
        if os.environ.get('AGENT_DEVICE_CLAIMS_DIR'):
            claims.append(Path(os.environ['AGENT_DEVICE_CLAIMS_DIR']))
        self.claim_dirs = claims
        self.grace = env_float('SIM_JANITOR_GRACE_MINUTES', 30.0) * 60
        # An open agent-device session with no activity for this long no
        # longer owns its device. agent-device's own idle timeout is off by
        # default, so without this a forgotten session pins it forever.
        self.session_cap = env_float('SIM_JANITOR_SESSION_IDLE_MINUTES', 120.0) * 60
        self.xcrun = os.environ.get('SIM_JANITOR_XCRUN') or '/usr/bin/xcrun'
        self.ps = os.environ.get('SIM_JANITOR_PS') or '/bin/ps'
        self.list_timeout = env_float('SIM_JANITOR_LIST_TIMEOUT', 45.0)
        self.ps_timeout = env_float('SIM_JANITOR_PS_TIMEOUT', 20.0)
        self.shutdown_timeout = env_float('SIM_JANITOR_SHUTDOWN_TIMEOUT', 90.0)
        # launchd starts a pass every 300s. A pass gives up well before that.
        self.pass_budget = env_float('SIM_JANITOR_PASS_BUDGET', 240.0)
        # Don't start a device's final check and shutdown with less than this
        # much of the budget left.
        self.min_step = env_float('SIM_JANITOR_MIN_STEP', 10.0)
        self.clock = time.time
        for key, value in overrides.items():
            if not hasattr(self, key):
                raise TypeError(f'unknown setting {key}')
            setattr(self, key, value)


# --- logging -----------------------------------------------------------------

def log(config, message):
    """Append one line to the log, rotating it at 1 MB. Never raises."""
    line = f'{time.strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S%z")} [{os.getpid()}] {message}\n'
    try:
        config.log_file.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
        try:
            if config.log_file.stat().st_size > LOG_LIMIT:
                config.log_file.replace(config.log_file.with_name(config.log_file.name + '.1'))
        except FileNotFoundError:
            pass
        with open(config.log_file, 'a') as output:
            output.write(line)
    except OSError:
        sys.stderr.write(line)


# --- subprocesses ------------------------------------------------------------

def call(args, timeout):
    """stdout of a command, or Unavailable. A command that overruns `timeout`
    is killed: it is our own child, never a simulator or a tool's process."""
    if timeout <= 0:
        raise Unavailable(f'{" ".join(args[:4])} skipped: no time left in the pass')
    try:
        result = subprocess.run(args, stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL, capture_output=True, text=True,
                                errors='replace', timeout=timeout, env=dict(os.environ, LC_ALL='C'))
    except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:
        raise Unavailable(f'{" ".join(args[:4])} timed out after {timeout:.0f}s') from None
    except OSError as error:
        raise Unavailable(f'{args[0]}: {error}') from None
    if result.returncode != 0:
        detail = (result.stderr or result.stdout).strip().splitlines()
        raise Unavailable(f'{" ".join(args[:4])} exited {result.returncode}'
                          + (f': {detail[-1][:200]}' if detail else ''))
    return result.stdout


def simctl_args(config, device_set, *args):
    return [config.xcrun, 'simctl', *(['--set', 'testing'] if device_set == 'testing' else []), *args]


def list_devices(config, device_set, timeout=None):
    """[{udid, name, state, set}] for every device in the set."""
    output = call(simctl_args(config, device_set, 'list', 'devices', '-j'),
                  config.list_timeout if timeout is None else timeout)
    try:
        groups = json.loads(output)['devices']
        devices = []
        for runtime, entries in groups.items():
            for entry in entries:
                if not UDID.fullmatch(entry['udid']):
                    raise ValueError(f'odd UDID {entry["udid"]!r}')
                devices.append(dict(udid=entry['udid'].upper(), name=entry['name'], state=entry['state'],
                                    set=device_set, runtime=runtime.rsplit('.', 1)[-1]))
        return devices
    except (ValueError, KeyError, TypeError, AttributeError) as error:
        raise Unavailable(f'simctl list ({device_set}) printed something unexpected: {error}') from None


class Process:
    __slots__ = ('pid', 'ppid', 'stat', 'start', 'command')

    def __init__(self, pid, ppid, stat, start, command):
        self.pid, self.ppid, self.stat, self.start, self.command = pid, ppid, stat, start, command


def process_table(config, timeout=None):
    """{pid: Process} for every process. `start` is ps's lstart, which is what
    agent-device records as a process's start time."""
    output = call([config.ps, '-axww', '-o', 'pid=,ppid=,stat=,lstart=,command='],
                  config.ps_timeout if timeout is None else timeout)
    table = {}
    for line in output.splitlines():
        fields = line.split(None, 8)
        if len(fields) < 8:
            continue
        if not (fields[0].isdigit() and fields[1].isdigit()):
            raise Unavailable(f'ps printed an unexpected line: {line[:120]!r}')
        pid = int(fields[0])
        table[pid] = Process(pid, int(fields[1]), fields[2], ' '.join(fields[3:8]),
                             fields[8] if len(fields) > 8 else '')
    if not table:
        raise Unavailable('ps listed no processes')
    return table


def parse_start(text):
    try:
        return time.mktime(time.strptime(' '.join(text.split()), '%a %b %d %H:%M:%S %Y'))
    except (ValueError, OverflowError):
        return None


# --- ownership ---------------------------------------------------------------

def is_runtime_root(process):
    argv0 = process.command.split(' ', 1)[0]
    return os.path.basename(argv0) == 'launchd_sim'


def device_trees(table):
    """{UDID: {pids}} of each device's launchd_sim and its descendants, and
    the set of every pid in any simulator's tree."""
    children = {}
    for process in table.values():
        children.setdefault(process.ppid, []).append(process.pid)
    trees, inside = {}, set()
    for root in table.values():
        if not is_runtime_root(root):
            continue
        match = re.search(r'/(?:Devices|XCTestDevices)/(' + UDID.pattern + r')/', root.command)
        tree = set()
        stack = [root.pid]
        while stack:
            pid = stack.pop()
            if pid in tree:
                continue
            tree.add(pid)
            stack.extend(children.get(pid, ()))
        inside |= tree
        if match:
            trees.setdefault(match[1].upper(), set()).update(tree)
    return trees, inside


def boot_times(table):
    """{UDID: epoch} from each launchd_sim's start time."""
    found = {}
    for process in table.values():
        if is_runtime_root(process):
            match = re.search(r'/(?:Devices|XCTestDevices)/(' + UDID.pattern + r')/', process.command)
            started = parse_start(process.start)
            if match and started is not None:
                found[match[1].upper()] = started
    return found


def is_agent_device_runner(command):
    argv0 = command.split(' ', 1)[0]
    return os.path.basename(argv0) == 'xcodebuild' and 'AgentDeviceRunner' in command


def is_app_or_test(command):
    return bool(BUNDLE_APP.search(command) or TEST_RUNNER.search(command))


def destination_names(command):
    """Every `name=` inside a `-destination` spec in a command line."""
    names = []
    for match in DESTINATION.finditer(command):
        rest = command[match.end():]
        if rest[:1] in ('"', "'"):
            end = rest.find(rest[0], 1)
            spec = rest[1:end] if end > 0 else rest[1:]
        else:
            stop = DESTINATION_END.search(rest)
            spec = rest[:stop.start()] if stop else rest
        for part in spec.split(','):
            key, sep, value = part.partition('=')
            if sep and key.strip() == 'name':
                value = value.strip().strip('\'"')
                if value:
                    names.append(value)
    return names


def session_dir_name(session):
    """agent-device's own mapping from a session name to its directory."""
    name = re.sub(r'[^a-zA-Z0-9._-]', '_', session)
    return name if name not in ('', '.', '..') else None


class Evidence:
    """What one look at the machine found: the process table and the claims.
    `problem` says why ownership cannot be judged at all this pass. `held` are
    the UDIDs whose lease files this process itself holds exclusively."""

    def __init__(self, config, table, problem=None, held=()):
        self.config = config
        self.table = table
        self.problem = problem
        self.held = {udid.upper() for udid in held}
        self.trees, self.inside = device_trees(table) if table else ({}, set())
        self.booted = boot_times(table) if table else {}
        self.named = self.destinations() if table else {}
        self.claims = self.read_claims() if table else []

    def destinations(self):
        named = {}
        for process in self.table.values():
            if process.pid in self.inside or process.pid == os.getpid() or '-destination' not in process.command:
                continue
            for name in destination_names(process.command):
                named.setdefault(name, []).append(process)
        return named

    def read_claims(self):
        claims = []
        now = self.config.clock()
        for directory in self.config.claim_dirs:
            try:
                names = sorted(os.listdir(directory))
            except FileNotFoundError:
                continue
            except OSError as error:
                self.problem = self.problem or f'agent-device claims in {directory} unreadable: {error}'
                continue
            for name in names:
                if not name.endswith('.json'):
                    continue
                path = Path(directory) / name
                try:
                    info = path.stat()
                    text = path.read_text(errors='replace') if info.st_size <= CLAIM_LIMIT else ''
                except OSError:
                    continue
                try:
                    claim = json.loads(text)
                    device = claim['device']['id'].upper()
                    pid = int(claim['ownerPid'])
                    started = claim.get('ownerStartTime')
                    updated = claim.get('updatedAtMs')
                    abandoned = claim.get('abandonedAtMs')
                    claims.append(dict(path=path, device=device, pid=pid, start=started,
                                       session=str(claim.get('session', '?')), readable=True,
                                       kind=claim.get('claimOwnerKind'), state_dir=claim.get('stateDir'),
                                       abandoned=abandoned / 1000 if isinstance(abandoned, (int, float)) else None,
                                       updated=updated / 1000 if isinstance(updated, (int, float)) else None))
                except (ValueError, KeyError, TypeError, AttributeError):
                    claims.append(dict(path=path, text=text.upper(), readable=False,
                                       fresh=now - info.st_mtime < UNREADABLE_CLAIM_WINDOW))
        return claims

    def session_activity(self, claim):
        """(epoch of the session's last activity, None), or (None, why) when a
        signal can't be read. The claim's updatedAtMs moves on open, renew and
        reboot takeover. The daemon appends to the session's events.ndjson as
        every request on it starts and finishes."""
        if claim['updated'] is None:
            return None, 'the claim has no updatedAtMs'
        state_dir, directory = claim['state_dir'], session_dir_name(claim['session'])
        if not isinstance(state_dir, str) or not os.path.isabs(state_dir) or directory is None:
            return None, 'the claim names no usable stateDir and session'
        events = Path(state_dir) / 'sessions' / directory / 'events.ndjson'
        try:
            touched = events.stat().st_mtime
        except OSError as error:
            return None, f'{events}: {error.strerror or error}'
        return max(claim['updated'], touched), None

    def claim_owners(self, udid):
        owners, notes = [], []
        now = self.config.clock()
        for claim in self.claims:
            if not claim['readable']:
                if udid in claim['text']:
                    if claim['fresh']:
                        owners.append(f'agent-device claim {claim["path"].name} (being written)')
                    else:
                        notes.append(f'unreadable agent-device claim {claim["path"].name}, ignored')
                continue
            if claim['device'] != udid:
                continue
            session = f'agent-device session {claim["session"]}'
            if claim['abandoned'] is not None:
                notes.append(f'{session}: closed {duration(max(0, now - claim["abandoned"]))} ago (claim abandoned)')
                continue
            owner = self.table.get(claim['pid'])
            if owner is None:
                notes.append(f'{session}: daemon {claim["pid"]} is gone')
                continue
            if isinstance(claim['start'], str) and claim['start'].split() != owner.start.split():
                notes.append(f'{session}: pid {claim["pid"]} was reused')
                continue
            who = f'{session} (daemon {claim["pid"]})'
            if claim['kind'] == 'transient-command':
                owners.append(f'{who}, running one command')
                continue
            last, why = self.session_activity(claim)
            if last is None:
                owners.append(f'{who}, last activity unknown ({why}), so counted as in use')
            elif now - last > self.config.session_cap:
                notes.append(f'{who}: last activity {duration(max(0, now - last))} ago, '
                             f'past the {duration(self.config.session_cap)} session cap')
            else:
                owners.append(f'{who}, last activity {duration(max(0, now - last))} ago')
        return owners, notes

    def process_owners(self, udid, name=None):
        owners, notes = [], []
        own_paths = re.compile(r'/(?:Devices|XCTestDevices)/' + udid, re.IGNORECASE)
        counted = set()
        for process in self.table.values():
            if process.pid in self.inside or process.pid == os.getpid():
                continue
            # A path inside the device's data directory isn't a use of the
            # device. Tools that drive one name its UDID.
            if udid not in own_paths.sub('', process.command).upper():
                continue
            if is_agent_device_runner(process.command):
                notes.append(f'agent-device runner {process.pid} (an owner only while its session is open)')
                continue
            counted.add(process.pid)
            owners.append(f'process {process.pid}: {process.command[:160]}')
        for process in self.named.get(name, ()) if name else ():
            if process.pid not in counted:
                counted.add(process.pid)
                owners.append(f'process {process.pid} names it {name!r} in -destination: {process.command[:140]}')
        for pid in sorted(self.trees.get(udid, ())):
            process = self.table.get(pid)
            if process and 'X' in process.stat:
                owners.append(f'process {pid} is being debugged: {process.command[:140]}')
        return owners, notes

    def activity(self, udid):
        """(epoch, Process) of the newest app or test process in the device's
        own tree, or None. Its start time, not its existence, is the activity."""
        newest = None
        for pid in self.trees.get(udid, ()):
            process = self.table.get(pid)
            if process is None or not is_app_or_test(process.command):
                continue
            started = parse_start(process.start)
            if started is not None and (newest is None or started > newest[0]):
                newest = (started, process)
        return newest

    def owners(self, udid, name=None):
        """(owners, notes) for one UDID, named `name`. Owners mark it in use."""
        owners, notes = [], []
        if udid.upper() not in self.held and lease_held(self.config, udid):
            owners.append(f'lease {lease_path(self.config, udid)}')
        for found, noted in (self.process_owners(udid, name), self.claim_owners(udid)):
            owners += found
            notes += noted
        return owners, notes


def lease_path(config, udid):
    return config.lease_dir / f'{udid.upper()}.lock'


def lease_held(config, udid):
    """Whether any `sim-janitor lease` holds this device. Never creates the file."""
    try:
        handle = open(lease_path(config, udid), 'rb')
    except OSError:
        return False
    with handle:
        try:
            fcntl.flock(handle, fcntl.LOCK_EX | fcntl.LOCK_NB)
        except OSError:
            return True
        fcntl.flock(handle, fcntl.LOCK_UN)
    return False


def lock_leases(config, udids):
    """Exclusive, non-blocking locks on these devices' lease files, created if
    missing. Returns (handles, None), or (None, UDID) when a lease holds one.
    While these are held a `sim-janitor lease` on any of them waits."""
    config.lease_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    handles = []
    for udid in sorted({udid.upper() for udid in udids}):
        try:
            handle = open(lease_path(config, udid), 'a+')
        except OSError:
            release_leases(handles)
            raise
        try:
            fcntl.flock(handle, fcntl.LOCK_EX | fcntl.LOCK_NB)
        except OSError as error:
            handle.close()
            release_leases(handles)
            if error.errno in (errno.EWOULDBLOCK, errno.EAGAIN):
                return None, udid
            raise
        handles.append(handle)
    return handles, None


def release_leases(handles, outcome=None):
    """Record what the janitor did in each lease file, for a lease that waited
    on it, then unlock."""
    for handle in handles:
        if outcome is not None:
            try:
                handle.seek(0)
                handle.truncate()
                handle.write(json.dumps(outcome) + '\n')
                handle.flush()
            except OSError:
                pass
        handle.close()


def related(device, by_name):
    """(UDID, name) pairs whose owners also own `device`: a testing-set clone
    is owned through the default-set device it was cloned from."""
    pairs = [(device['udid'], device['name'])]
    if device['set'] == 'testing':
        match = CLONE.fullmatch(device['name'])
        if match:
            pairs += [(udid, match[1]) for udid in by_name.get(match[1], ()) if udid != device['udid']]
    return pairs


def look(config, held=(), timeout=None):
    try:
        return Evidence(config, process_table(config, timeout), held=held)
    except Unavailable as error:
        return Evidence(config, None, f'process table unreadable: {error}')


# --- state -------------------------------------------------------------------

def load_state(config):
    """{since: {key: epoch}, attempts: {key: {last, failures}}}. `since` is
    when each device was last seen owned (or first seen), `attempts` its run
    of failed shutdowns."""
    state = dict(since={}, attempts={})
    try:
        data = json.loads(config.state_file.read_text())
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        return state
    try:
        state['since'] = {str(key): float(value) for key, value in data.get('since', {}).items()}
    except (AttributeError, TypeError, ValueError):
        pass
    try:
        for key, entry in data.get('attempts', {}).items():
            state['attempts'][str(key)] = dict(last=float(entry['last']), failures=int(entry['failures']))
    except (AttributeError, TypeError, ValueError, KeyError):
        state['attempts'] = {}
    return state


def save_state(config, state):
    config.state_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    temporary = config.state_file.with_name(f'.state.{os.getpid()}.tmp')
    temporary.write_text(json.dumps(state, indent=1, sort_keys=True) + '\n')
    os.replace(temporary, config.state_file)


def key_of(device):
    return f'{device["set"]}:{device["udid"]}'


def backoff_left(entry, now):
    """Seconds until a device whose shutdowns keep failing is tried again."""
    if not entry or entry['failures'] < 2:
        return 0
    wait = min(BACKOFF_BASE * 2 ** (entry['failures'] - 2), BACKOFF_MAX)
    return max(0.0, entry['last'] + wait - now)


# --- one pass ----------------------------------------------------------------

def inventory(config, sets=('default', 'testing'), timeout=None):
    """(devices, sets that listed, problems). Without the default set nothing is known."""
    devices, listed, problems = [], [], []
    for device_set in sets:
        try:
            devices += list_devices(config, device_set, timeout)
            listed.append(device_set)
        except Unavailable as error:
            problems.append(str(error))
            if device_set == 'default':
                break
    return devices, listed, problems


def judge(config, devices, evidence, since, now, keys=None):
    """One verdict per booted device (or per key in `keys`): dict(device,
    owners, notes, idle, activity, action). Updates `since` with what was seen."""
    by_name = {}
    for device in devices:
        if device['set'] == 'default':
            by_name.setdefault(device['name'], []).append(device['udid'])
    verdicts = []
    for device in devices:
        if device['state'] != 'Booted':
            continue
        key = key_of(device)
        if keys is not None and key not in keys:
            continue
        owners, notes = [], []
        activity = None
        if evidence.problem is None:
            for udid, name in related(device, by_name):
                found, noted = evidence.owners(udid, name)
                suffix = '' if udid == device['udid'] else f' (via source {udid})'
                owners += [owner + suffix for owner in found]
                notes += [note + suffix for note in noted]
            activity = evidence.activity(device['udid'])
        if owners:
            since[key] = now
        elif key not in since:
            since[key] = now
        if activity is not None and activity[0] > since[key]:
            # An app or test runner started since: idle from that start.
            since[key] = min(activity[0], now)
        started = max(since[key], evidence.booted.get(device['udid'], 0))
        idle = max(0.0, now - started)
        if evidence.problem is not None:
            action = f'keep: cannot judge ({evidence.problem})'
        elif owners:
            action = 'keep: in use'
        elif idle >= config.grace:
            action = 'shut down'
        else:
            action = f'keep: shut down in {duration(config.grace - idle)} if still idle'
        verdicts.append(dict(device=device, owners=owners, notes=notes, idle=idle, activity=activity,
                             action=action))
    return verdicts


def duration(seconds):
    seconds = int(seconds)
    if seconds < 60:
        return f'{seconds}s'
    if seconds < 3600:
        return f'{seconds // 60}m'
    return f'{seconds // 3600}h{seconds % 3600 // 60:02d}m'


def label(device):
    return f'{device["name"]} ({device["udid"]}, {device["set"]} set)'


def shutdown(config, device, timeout):
    call(simctl_args(config, device['set'], 'shutdown', device['udid']), timeout)


def run_pass(config, dry_run=False):
    """One pass. Returns the exit status. Assumes the single-instance lock is held."""
    began = config.clock()
    deadline = time.monotonic() + config.pass_budget
    tag = '[dry-run] ' if dry_run else ''
    devices, listed, problems = inventory(config)
    for problem in problems:
        log(config, f'{tag}{problem}')
    if 'default' not in listed:
        log(config, f'{tag}pass done: simctl could not list devices, nothing judged')
        return 1
    state = load_state(config)
    since, attempts = state['since'], state['attempts']
    evidence = look(config)
    if evidence.problem:
        log(config, f'{tag}{evidence.problem}; keeping every device this pass')
    now = config.clock()
    verdicts = judge(config, devices, evidence, since, now)
    candidates = [v for v in verdicts if v['action'] == 'shut down']
    booted = {key_of(v['device']) for v in verdicts}

    def forget():
        # Forget devices that are no longer booted in the sets that listed.
        for table in (since, attempts):
            for key in list(table):
                if key.split(':', 1)[0] in listed and key not in booted:
                    del table[key]

    def save():
        try:
            save_state(config, state)
        except OSError as error:
            log(config, f'could not save state: {error}')

    counts = dict(shut=0, failed=0, waiting=0)
    stopped = ''
    if candidates:
        if dry_run:
            for verdict in candidates:
                wait = backoff_left(attempts.get(key_of(verdict['device'])), now)
                log(config, f'{tag}would shut down {label(verdict["device"])}, idle {duration(verdict["idle"])}'
                            + (f', after a back-off of {duration(wait)}' if wait else ''))
        else:
            forget()
            counts, stopped = shut_down(config, candidates, state, deadline, save)
    forget()
    if not dry_run:
        save()
    in_use = sum(1 for v in verdicts if v['owners'])
    log(config, f'{tag}pass done: {len(verdicts)} booted, {in_use} in use, '
                f'{len(candidates)} idle past {duration(config.grace)}, {counts["shut"]} shut down, '
                f'{counts["failed"]} failed, {counts["waiting"]} waiting'
                f'{"" if "testing" in listed else ", testing set unlisted"}'
                f'{f", stopped: {stopped}" if stopped else ""}; '
                f'took {config.clock() - began:.1f}s')
    return 1 if counts['failed'] else 0


def shut_down(config, candidates, state, deadline, save):
    """Shut down each candidate that is still idle when checked again right
    before acting. Tries devices that never failed first, then the least
    recently failed, and skips one backing off. Returns (counts, why it
    stopped early or '')."""
    since, attempts = state['since'], state['attempts']
    counts = dict(shut=0, failed=0, waiting=0)
    now = config.clock()

    def order(verdict):
        key = key_of(verdict['device'])
        return (attempts[key]['last'] if key in attempts else 0, -verdict['idle'], key)

    queue = sorted(candidates, key=order)
    for index, verdict in enumerate(queue):
        device = verdict['device']
        key = key_of(device)
        left = len(queue) - index
        if config.pause_file.exists():
            log(config, f'paused: {config.pause_file} appeared, {left} device(s) left booted')
            counts['waiting'] += left
            return counts, 'paused'
        wait = backoff_left(attempts.get(key), now)
        if wait > 0:
            counts['waiting'] += 1
            log(config, f'{label(device)} failed to shut down {attempts[key]["failures"]} times in a row, '
                        f'next try in {duration(wait)}')
            continue
        if deadline - time.monotonic() < config.min_step:
            log(config, f'pass budget spent, {left} device(s) wait for the next pass')
            counts['waiting'] += left
            return counts, 'budget spent'
        result = shut_down_one(config, device, since, deadline)
        if result == 'shut':
            counts['shut'] += 1
            attempts.pop(key, None)
        elif result == 'failed':
            counts['failed'] += 1
            previous = attempts.get(key, dict(failures=0))
            attempts[key] = dict(last=config.clock(), failures=previous['failures'] + 1)
        elif result == 'gone':
            attempts.pop(key, None)
        elif result == 'paused':
            counts['waiting'] += left
            return counts, 'paused'
        elif result == 'unchecked':
            counts['waiting'] += 1
        # Persist as we go, so a hard stop mid-pass keeps the failure counts.
        save()
    return counts, ''


def shut_down_one(config, device, since, deadline):
    """Lock the device's leases, judge it again from scratch, and shut it down
    if it is still idle. The locks are held until simctl returns. Returns
    'shut', 'failed', 'kept', 'gone', 'paused' or 'unchecked'."""
    key = key_of(device)

    def left():
        return deadline - time.monotonic()

    sets = ('default',) if device['set'] == 'default' else ('default', device['set'])
    current, listed, problems = inventory(config, sets, min(config.list_timeout, left()))
    if device['set'] not in listed or 'default' not in listed:
        log(config, f'kept {label(device)} this pass: cannot list devices ({"; ".join(problems)})')
        return 'unchecked'
    now_device = next((d for d in current if key_of(d) == key), None)
    if now_device is None or now_device['state'] != 'Booted':
        return 'gone'
    by_name = {}
    for each in current:
        if each['set'] == 'default':
            by_name.setdefault(each['name'], []).append(each['udid'])
    udids = [udid for udid, _ in related(now_device, by_name)]
    try:
        handles, busy = lock_leases(config, udids)
    except OSError as error:
        log(config, f'kept {label(device)} this pass: cannot lock its lease file: {error}')
        return 'unchecked'
    if handles is None:
        since[key] = config.clock()
        log(config, f'kept {label(device)}: an owner arrived (lease on {busy})')
        return 'kept'
    outcome = None
    try:
        evidence = look(config, held=udids, timeout=min(config.ps_timeout, left()))
        if evidence.problem:
            log(config, f'kept {label(device)} this pass: {evidence.problem}')
            return 'unchecked'
        verdict = judge(config, current, evidence, since, config.clock(), keys={key})[0]
        if verdict['action'] != 'shut down':
            if verdict['owners']:
                log(config, f'kept {label(device)}: an owner arrived ({verdict["owners"][0][:120]})')
            else:
                log(config, f'kept {label(device)}: idle only {duration(verdict["idle"])} now')
            outcome = dict(result='kept', at=time.time(), pid=os.getpid())
            return 'kept'
        if config.pause_file.exists():
            log(config, f'paused: {config.pause_file} appeared, {label(device)} left booted')
            return 'paused'
        timeout = min(config.shutdown_timeout, left())
        try:
            shutdown(config, device, timeout)
        except Unavailable as error:
            log(config, f'could not shut down {label(device)}: {error}')
            outcome = dict(result='failed', at=time.time(), pid=os.getpid(), error=str(error)[:200])
            return 'failed'
        since.pop(key, None)
        log(config, f'shut down {label(device)} after {duration(verdict["idle"])} idle')
        outcome = dict(result='shut down', at=time.time(), pid=os.getpid())
        return 'shut'
    finally:
        release_leases(handles, outcome)


# --- commands ----------------------------------------------------------------

def acquire_instance_lock(config):
    """The open lock file, or None when another pass holds it."""
    config.state_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    handle = open(config.lock_file, 'a+')
    try:
        fcntl.flock(handle, fcntl.LOCK_EX | fcntl.LOCK_NB)
    except OSError as error:
        handle.close()
        if error.errno in (errno.EWOULDBLOCK, errno.EAGAIN):
            return None
        raise
    handle.seek(0)
    handle.truncate()
    handle.write(f'{os.getpid()}\n')
    handle.flush()
    return handle


def holder(config):
    try:
        return config.lock_file.read_text().strip() or '?'
    except OSError:
        return '?'


def on_alarm(signum, frame):
    raise PassDeadline()


def command_run(config, dry_run=False):
    tag = '[dry-run] ' if dry_run else ''
    if config.pause_file.exists():
        log(config, f'{tag}paused: {config.pause_file} exists, doing nothing')
        return 0
    try:
        lock = acquire_instance_lock(config)
    except OSError as error:
        log(config, f'{tag}cannot take the single-instance lock: {error}')
        return 1
    if lock is None:
        log(config, f'{tag}another pass is running (pid {holder(config)}), exiting')
        return 0
    # A hard stop for the whole pass, beyond each subprocess's own timeout.
    previous = signal.signal(signal.SIGALRM, on_alarm)
    signal.alarm(int(config.pass_budget + config.shutdown_timeout + 30))
    try:
        return run_pass(config, dry_run)
    except PassDeadline:
        log(config, f'{tag}pass hit its hard deadline and stopped')
        return 1
    except Exception as error:  # noqa: BLE001 - a crash must still leave a log line
        log(config, f'{tag}pass failed: {type(error).__name__}: {error} | '
                    + ' / '.join(traceback.format_exc().strip().splitlines()[-3:]))
        return 1
    finally:
        signal.alarm(0)
        signal.signal(signal.SIGALRM, previous)
        lock.close()


def command_status(config, out=None):
    out = out or sys.stdout
    devices, listed, problems = inventory(config)
    for problem in problems:
        print(f'warning: {problem}', file=out)
    if 'default' not in listed:
        print('simctl could not list devices', file=out)
        return 1
    state = load_state(config)
    evidence = look(config)
    if evidence.problem:
        print(f'warning: {evidence.problem}', file=out)
    paused = config.pause_file.exists()
    print(f'grace {duration(config.grace)}; agent-device session cap {duration(config.session_cap)}; '
          f'log {config.log_file}; leases {config.lease_dir}'
          + (f'; PAUSED by {config.pause_file}' if paused else ''), file=out)
    now = config.clock()
    verdicts = judge(config, devices, evidence, state['since'], now)
    if not verdicts:
        print('no booted devices', file=out)
    for verdict in verdicts:
        device = verdict['device']
        boot = evidence.booted.get(device['udid'])
        up = f', up {duration(now - boot)}' if boot else ''
        print(f'{label(device)} {device["runtime"]}{up}', file=out)
        if not verdict['owners']:
            print('    owners: none found', file=out)
        for owner in verdict['owners']:
            print(f'    owner: {owner}', file=out)
        for note in verdict['notes']:
            print(f'    not an owner: {note}', file=out)
        if verdict['activity']:
            started, process = verdict['activity']
            print(f'    last app or test start: {duration(max(0, now - started))} ago, '
                  f'process {process.pid}: {process.command[:120]}', file=out)
        action = verdict['action']
        if paused and action == 'shut down':
            action = 'shut down (once unpaused)'
        entry = state['attempts'].get(key_of(device))
        if entry:
            wait = backoff_left(entry, now)
            action += (f'; {entry["failures"]} failed shutdown(s) in a row'
                       + (f', next try in {duration(wait)}' if wait else ''))
        print(f'    idle {duration(verdict["idle"])} -> {action}', file=out)
    return 0


def command_lease(config, udid, command):
    if not UDID.fullmatch(udid):
        print(f'sim-janitor lease: {udid!r} is not a simulator UDID', file=sys.stderr)
        return 64
    if not command:
        print('sim-janitor lease: nothing to run (sim-janitor lease UDID -- COMMAND...)', file=sys.stderr)
        return 64
    config.lease_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    with open(lease_path(config, udid), 'a+') as handle:
        # Shared, so several tools can hold one device at once. The janitor's
        # exclusive probe fails while any of them runs. While the janitor
        # holds its exclusive lock to shut this device down, wait for it: at
        # most one final check and one shutdown timeout.
        if not try_shared_lock(handle):
            began = time.time()
            print(f'sim-janitor lease: waiting for sim-janitor, which is checking {udid.upper()} '
                  'for shutdown', file=sys.stderr)
            fcntl.flock(handle, fcntl.LOCK_SH)
            report_janitor(handle, udid, began)
        try:
            child = subprocess.Popen(command)
        except OSError as error:
            print(f'sim-janitor lease: {command[0]}: {error}', file=sys.stderr)
            return 127

        def forward(signum, frame):
            try:
                child.send_signal(signum)
            except OSError:
                pass

        # The terminal already sends SIGINT to the whole process group, so the
        # lease only has to outlive the command rather than die first and drop
        # the lock. Set after Popen, since an ignored signal survives exec.
        signal.signal(signal.SIGINT, signal.SIG_IGN)
        for each in (signal.SIGTERM, signal.SIGHUP):
            signal.signal(each, forward)
        while True:
            try:
                status = child.wait()
                break
            except InterruptedError:
                continue
    return status if status >= 0 else 128 - status


def try_shared_lock(handle):
    """A shared lock without waiting, retried briefly so the janitor's
    momentary ownership probe doesn't count as a shutdown in progress."""
    for attempt in range(5):
        try:
            fcntl.flock(handle, fcntl.LOCK_SH | fcntl.LOCK_NB)
            return True
        except OSError as error:
            if error.errno not in (errno.EWOULDBLOCK, errno.EAGAIN):
                raise
        time.sleep(0.05)
    return False


def report_janitor(handle, udid, began):
    """After waiting on the janitor, say on stderr what it did to the device."""
    try:
        handle.seek(0)
        outcome = json.loads(handle.read() or '{}')
        result, at = outcome.get('result'), float(outcome.get('at', 0))
    except (OSError, ValueError, TypeError, AttributeError):
        return
    if at < began - 1:
        return
    if result == 'shut down':
        print(f'sim-janitor lease: sim-janitor shut {udid.upper()} down while this lease waited; '
              'the command runs anyway, so boot the device if it needs one', file=sys.stderr)
    elif result == 'failed':
        print(f'sim-janitor lease: sim-janitor tried to shut {udid.upper()} down while this lease waited '
              'and simctl did not confirm it; the device may be shutting down', file=sys.stderr)


def main(argv=None, config=None):
    argv = sys.argv[1:] if argv is None else argv
    if argv[:1] == ['lease']:
        rest = argv[1:]
        if len(rest) < 2 or rest[1] != '--':
            print('usage: sim-janitor lease UDID -- COMMAND...', file=sys.stderr)
            return 64
        return command_lease(config or Config(), rest[0], rest[2:])
    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(prog='sim-janitor', description=__doc__.split('\n\n')[0])
    commands = parser.add_subparsers(dest='command')
    run = commands.add_parser('run', help='one pass, then exit')
    run.add_argument('--dry-run', action='store_true', help='decide and log, but shut nothing down')
    status = commands.add_parser('status', help='booted devices, their owners, and what run would do')
    for each in (run, status):
        each.add_argument('--grace-minutes', type=float, help='idle minutes before shutdown (default 30)')
        each.add_argument('--session-idle-minutes', type=float,
                          help='minutes without activity before an agent-device session stops '
                               'owning its device (default 120)')
    commands.add_parser('lease', help='sim-janitor lease UDID -- COMMAND...: hold the device while COMMAND runs')
    args = parser.parse_args(argv)
    if args.command is None:
        parser.print_help()
        return 64
    config = config or Config()
    if args.grace_minutes is not None:
        config.grace = args.grace_minutes * 60
    if args.session_idle_minutes is not None:
        config.session_cap = args.session_idle_minutes * 60
    if args.command == 'run':
        return command_run(config, args.dry_run)
    return command_status(config)


if __name__ == '__main__':
    sys.exit(main())
